# A case-class `Array` field, indexed directly off the receiver

Executable record of BUGS.md `case-class-array-field-cannot-be-indexed-directly`. The
entry had NO gate, so nothing would have told anyone if it were fixed — or if it got
worse. This case is that gate: it is declared `known-red` on the lanes that fail today,
and the suite turns RED the moment the defect goes away, which is what forces whoever
fixes it to come back here and delete the declaration.

`b.arr(0)` is an index on a field read straight off the receiver. Binding the field to a
local first works, so the defect is specifically the direct form.

```scalascript
case class Box(arr: Array[Int])

def main(): Unit =
  val b = Box(Array(1, 2, 3))
  val a = b.arr
  println(a(0))
  println(b.arr(0))

main()
```
